WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.630
- I have to say again it
was great to sing your music

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.390
last week at the Academy
of Country Music Awards.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.380
But I will say it's always, always, always

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.370
going to be terrifying to sing your song

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.010
in front of you while you're there.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.677
Just so you know, I'm
always sweating profusely.

00:00:14.677 --> 00:00:15.510
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.740
- Oh, well, I mean

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.040
I don't think you have to
worry with a voice like yours.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.030
I was so honored
(audience cheering)

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.900
and nobody can sing like you.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.930
So I was very proud of of you

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.890
and so proud of your rendition of it.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:26.723
It's great.

00:00:26.723 --> 00:00:28.960
One of the best ever, ever, ever.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.850
- You are so kind.
(audience cheering)

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.520
And it was also

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:33.507
we haven't really been
able to talk about it

00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:35.310
but it was cool to sing "9 to 5"

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.270
We did the kind of reimagined version

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.700
of "9 to 5" for your documentary

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.260
still working "9 to 5", which is amazing.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.900
Not just the song, but the
documentary is amazing.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.290
So thank you for letting
me be a part of that.

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:48.138
I got to brag to Blake
Shelton about that moment.

00:00:48.138 --> 00:00:50.230
(kelly laughs)

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.430
- Well, you did a great job on that too.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.810
I love how you took that
and just made it your own.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:58.060
And I got a chance to sing
background for a change

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.250
but I'm really proud of
that rendition of it.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.530
And I think hopefully
it'll do well for us.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:03.757
It's great in the documentary.

00:01:03.757 --> 00:01:04.590
(audience cheering)

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:05.423
- Oh my God.

00:01:05.423 --> 00:01:06.470
It's a really cool thing.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:09.143
James, do you have a favorite Dolly song?

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.650
- Yeah, well, first of all

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.800
off of the new album, "Run Rose Run."

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.752
I love "Big Dreams And Faded Jeans"

00:01:15.752 --> 00:01:18.350
and "Woman Up (And Take It Like A Man)".

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:19.243
Right?

00:01:19.243 --> 00:01:20.076
- I love that one.

00:01:20.076 --> 00:01:20.909
I love-

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:22.397
(kelly laughing)
- Yeah.

00:01:22.397 --> 00:01:24.467
He has always loved that one.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.762
- "My Life Would Suck Without
You", I love that one.

00:01:26.762 --> 00:01:27.595
- Yes.

00:01:27.595 --> 00:01:28.483
- Yes Kelly.

00:01:29.362 --> 00:01:30.490
- Yes.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.163
- James Patterson knows our music.

00:01:32.163 --> 00:01:32.996
(audience cheering)

